---
import { cityGroups, homeFaqs } from "../../lib/seo/homeContent";
---

<div class="atlas-seo">
  <section aria-labelledby="how-world-clock-works">
    <h2 id="how-world-clock-works">How this world clock works</h2>
    <p>
      Search a city or a country to see the current time there, beside your own. Add more than one
      place when you need the time difference for a call, a flight, or a deadline. Every clock uses
      your device's time and the IANA time zone for that place, so UTC offsets and daylight saving
      time follow the rules in effect today.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prefer a list to the globe?
      <a href="/clocks/">Browse world clocks by country</a>, or read how
      <a href="/guide/">time zones, UTC, GMT, and daylight saving</a> actually work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="current-time-cities">
    <h2 id="current-time-cities">Current time in major cities</h2>
    <p>
      These are the places people look up most often. Search any of them above for the current local
      time, the UTC offset, and whether daylight saving time is in effect.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        cityGroups.map((group) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{group.region}.</strong> {group.places}.
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>
      There is no single current time for the United States, Canada, Russia, or Australia. Pick the
      city. For a zero offset, search UTC.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="time-zone-questions">
    <h2 id="time-zone-questions">Time zone questions</h2>
    <dl>
      {
        homeFaqs.map((item) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{item.question}</dt>
            <dd>{item.answer}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>
</div>
